60,3,1,talk,May,,"Okay, we have the options. A is rotating, B is managed hours, and C is a structure. Given the complaints, A seems the most fair.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,I disagree with C because of the smell and the fights Midori found. B seems too rigid with that early truck arrival time.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option C is way too expensive! Even with the subsidy, it's a huge hit to the budget. I'm leaning towards A or B.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm scared of B because of the ""policing"" issue. A seems like it could be fair, but will moving the bins cause new arguments?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option C requires too much administrative labor and long-term maintenance. Option B places a heavy burden on the early riser.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, moving the bins is better than one person suffering for years. The complaint log proves the current spot is a disaster.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, I agree. Rotating the location means no one is stuck with the smell or the blockage forever. It's the most logical compromise.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"If we go with A, we don't have to pay for a big expensive building! It saves us money and solves the fairness problem.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Midori,,"If everyone agrees that rotating is the kindest way to share the burden, then I can support it. I just want us to stay friends.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,Rotation is a natural cycle. It prevents the stagnation of resentment and ensures that no single soul bears the weight alone.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,I'm voting for A. It's the only one that actually addresses the unfairness of the current location.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for A. It avoids the hygiene issues of a structure and the social friction of supervised hours.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I vote for A! It's the cheapest and it's fair. Let's do it!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'll vote for A too. As long as we all agree to the rotation, it seems like the most harmonious choice.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,I concur. Option A distributes the burden of time and space most equitably. I vote for A.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
